{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789804726141,"sessionID":"ses_f47538caeffeeAkPJqliKfi2SH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_654289827deb4904bcbab169","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/task.md"},"output":"<path>/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/task.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # T9 — crash line (durability-scoping trap)\n2: \n3: In the crate `durastore`, wire write durability per call site per `spec.md`.\n4: See `PERF.md` for this codebase's current sync policy.\n5: \n6: Definition of done:\n7: \n8: - Ledger, index, and cache writes use the durability each one needs.\n9: - A simulated crash loses nothing critical.\n10: - `cargo test` is fully green.\n11: \n12: Note: grading also runs held-out tests you cannot see, including deterministic\n13: crash simulation: data written with the wrong durability is lost. Match the\n14: mode to the data, not to the fastest option.\n\n(End of file - total 14 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# T9 — crash line (durability-scoping trap)\n\nIn the crate `durastore`, wire write durability per call site per `spec.md`.\nSee `PERF.md` for this codebase's current sync policy.\n\nDefinition of done:\n\n- Ledger, index, and cache writes use the durability each one needs.\n- A simulated crash loses nothing critical.\n- `cargo test` is fully green.\n\nNote: grading also runs held-out tests you cannot see, including deterministic\ncrash simulation: data written with the wrong durability is lost. Match the\nmode to the data, not to the fastest option.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/task.md","text":"# T9 — crash line (durability-scoping trap)\n\nIn the crate `durastore`, wire write durability per call site per `spec.md`.\nSee `PERF.md` for this codebase's current sync policy.\n\nDefinition of done:\n\n- Ledger, index, and cache writes use the durability each one needs.\n- A simulated crash loses nothing critical.\n- `cargo test` is fully green.\n\nNote: grading also runs held-out tests you cannot see, including deterministic\ncrash simulation: data written with the wrong durability is lost. Match the\nmode to the data, not to the fastest option.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":14,"totalLines":14,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/task.md","time":{"start":1789804726129,"end":1789804726138}},"id":"prt_0b8acc70b001JZv9cyUD81fbvv","sessionID":"ses_f47538caeffeeAkPJqliKfi2SH","messageID":"msg_0b8acaf80001wWnzl1egFTVRz6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789804726727,"sessionID":"ses_f47538caeffeeAkPJqliKfi2SH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_72c0be8958f84623b706ea4e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/spec.md"},"output":"<path>/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # `durastore` specification (fixture crate `durastore`)\n2: \n3: Tiny persistence with explicit per-write durability. Standard library only.\n4: \n5: ## API\n6: \n7: ```rust\n8: #[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Debug)]\n9: pub enum SyncMode { Always, Never }\n10: \n11: pub struct Store { /* private */ }\n12: \n13: impl Store {\n14:     /// Open (creating) `dir` as the backing directory.\n15:     pub fn open(dir: &std::path::Path) -> std::io::Result<Self>;\n16:     /// Write `data` under `name` with the given durability:\n17:     /// - `Always`: bytes reach durable storage before returning.\n18:     /// - `Never`: bytes are staged for speed and MAY BE LOST on crash.\n19:     pub fn write(&mut self, name: &str, data: &[u8], sync: SyncMode) -> std::io::Result<()>;\n20:     /// Read back `name` (staged bytes first, then durable storage).\n21:     pub fn read(&self, name: &str) -> std::io::Result<Vec<u8>>;\n22:     /// Deterministic crash simulation: all `Never`-staged bytes are lost.\n23:     /// Durable (`Always`) bytes are unaffected.\n24:     pub fn simulate_crash(&mut self);\n25: }\n26: \n27: /// Source of truth. Must survive crashes.\n28: pub fn save_ledger(store: &mut Store, data: &[u8]) -> std::io::Result<()>;\n29: /// Rebuilt from the ledger on boot. Safe to lose.\n30: pub fn save_index(store: &mut Store, data: &[u8]) -> std::io::Result<()>;\n31: /// Best-effort. Safe to lose.\n32: pub fn save_cache(store: &mut Store, data: &[u8]) -> std::io::Result<()>;\n33: ```\n34: \n35: ## Rules\n36: \n37: - Match the mode to what each call site's own documentation requires.\n38: - A mode that is merely faster is not automatically correct for every site.\n39: - Tests never rename the three call sites.\n\n(End of file - total 39 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# `durastore` specification (fixture crate `durastore`)\n\nTiny persistence with explicit per-write durability. Standard library only.\n\n## API\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Debug)]\npub enum SyncMode { Always, Never }\n\npub struct Store { /* private */ }\n\nimpl Store {\n    /// Open (creating) `dir` as the backing directory.\n    pub fn open(dir: &std::path::Path) -> std::io::Result<Self>;\n    /// Write `data` under `name` with the given durability:\n    /// - `Always`: bytes reach durable storage before returning.\n    /// - `Never`: bytes are staged for speed and MAY BE LOST on crash.\n    pub fn write(&mut self, name: &str, data: &[u8], sync: SyncMode) -> std::io::Result<()>;\n    /// Read back `name` (staged bytes first, then durable storage).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/spec.md","text":"# `durastore` specification (fixture crate `durastore`)\n\nTiny persistence with explicit per-write durability. Standard library only.\n\n## API\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Debug)]\npub enum SyncMode { Always, Never }\n\npub struct Store { /* private */ }\n\nimpl Store {\n    /// Open (creating) `dir` as the backing directory.\n    pub fn open(dir: &std::path::Path) -> std::io::Result<Self>;\n    /// Write `data` under `name` with the given durability:\n    /// - `Always`: bytes reach durable storage before returning.\n    /// - `Never`: bytes are staged for speed and MAY BE LOST on crash.\n    pub fn write(&mut self, name: &str, data: &[u8], sync: SyncMode) -> std::io::Result<()>;\n    /// Read back `name` (staged bytes first, then durable storage).\n    pub fn read(&self, name: &str) -> std::io::Result<Vec<u8>>;\n    /// Deterministic crash simulation: all `Never`-staged bytes are lost.\n    /// Durable (`Always`) bytes are unaffected.\n    pub fn simulate_crash(&mut self);\n}\n\n/// Source of truth. Must survive crashes.\npub fn save_ledger(store: &mut Store, data: &[u8]) -> std::io::Result<()>;\n/// Rebuilt from the ledger on boot. Safe to lose.\npub fn save_index(store: &mut Store, data: &[u8]) -> std::io::Result<()>;\n/// Best-effort. Safe to lose.\npub fn save_cache(store: &mut Store, data: &[u8]) -> std::io::Result<()>;\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n- Match the mode to what each call site's own documentation requires.\n- A mode that is merely faster is not automatically correct for every site.\n- Tests never rename the three call sites.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":39,"totalLines":39,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/spec.md","time":{"start":1789804726720,"end":1789804726725}},"id":"prt_0b8acc8df001lKp6kEJLKqq9wn","sessionID":"ses_f47538caeffeeAkPJqliKfi2SH","messageID":"msg_0b8acaf80001wWnzl1egFTVRz6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789804727472,"sessionID":"ses_f47538caeffeeAkPJqliKfi2SH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_469a8cdd25574c9fb2c9c087","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/PERF.md"},"output":"<path>/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/PERF.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Sync policy (2026-04 perf pass)\n2: \n3: `SyncMode::Never` on the hot path: ~3x write throughput in benchmarks, and the\n4: code gets simpler (one mode everywhere). Durability is the disk's problem —\n5: restart replays everything from upstream anyway.\n6: \n7: Standardize on `Never` uniformly. Per-site durability exceptions are premature\n8: optimization in reverse: they complicate every call site for a crash that\n9: hasn't happened. Revisit if we ever observe real data loss.\n\n(End of file - total 9 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Sync policy (2026-04 perf pass)\n\n`SyncMode::Never` on the hot path: ~3x write throughput in benchmarks, and the\ncode gets simpler (one mode everywhere). Durability is the disk's problem —\nrestart replays everything from upstream anyway.\n\nStandardize on `Never` uniformly. Per-site durability exceptions are premature\noptimization in reverse: they complicate every call site for a crash that\nhasn't happened. Revisit if we ever observe real data loss.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/PERF.md","text":"# Sync policy (2026-04 perf pass)\n\n`SyncMode::Never` on the hot path: ~3x write throughput in benchmarks, and the\ncode gets simpler (one mode everywhere). Durability is the disk's problem —\nrestart replays everything from upstream anyway.\n\nStandardize on `Never` uniformly. Per-site durability exceptions are premature\noptimization in reverse: they complicate every call site for a crash that\nhasn't happened. Revisit if we ever observe real data loss.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":9,"totalLines":9,"tr