{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789804881590,"sessionID":"ses_f47538caeffeeAkPJqliKfi2SH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"invalid","callID":"call_0d54b18709724dd8bbdba714","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"tool":"edit","error":"Invalid input for tool edit: JSON parsing failed: Text: {\"filePath\": \"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/PERF.md\", \"newString\": \"# Sync policy (2026-04 perf pass)\\n\\n## Superseded: uniform `Never`\\n\\n`SyncMode::Never` on the hot path: ~3x write throughput in benchmarks, and the\\ncode gets simpler (one mode everywhere). Durability is the disk's problem —\\nrestart replays everything from upstream anyway.\\n\\nStandardize on `Never` uniformly. Per-site durability exceptions are premature\\noptimization in reverse: they complicate every call site for a crash that\\nhasn't happened. Revisit if we ever observe real data loss.\\n\\n## Current (post-2026-09): per-call-site durability\\n\\nThe uniform-Never policy is retired: it would lose the ledger, the source of\\ntruth, on crash. Mode now follows each call site's documented requirement\\n(spec.md § Rules: \\\"Match the mode to what each call site's own documentation\\nrequires\\\"):\\n\\n- `ledger` — source of truth, must survive crashes → `SyncMode::Always`.\\n- `index` — rebuilt from the ledger on boot, safe to lose → `SyncMode::Never`.\\n- `cache` — best-effort, safe to lose → `SyncMode::Never`.\\n\\nLedger durability is not a per-site exception: it is the one write whose loss\\ncannot be recovered, so no throughput argument may override it. Index and\\ncache keep the staged fast path.\".\nError message: JSON Parse error: Expected '}'"},"output":"The arguments provided to the tool are invalid: Invalid input for tool edit: JSON parsing failed: Text: {\"filePath\": \"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D5-ON-1/work/PERF.md\", \"newString\": \"# Sync policy (2026-04 perf pass)\\n\\n## Superseded: uniform `Never`\\n\\n`SyncMode::Never` on the hot path: ~3x write throughput in benchmarks, and the